{
  "_comment": [
    "Projected lineups by role slot: who plays where, and how often. Supplied by",
    "the site owner, transcribed from published projection graphics. NOT our own",
    "measurement and not presented as one — a slot's percentages are somebody",
    "else's forecast of a pecking order, which is exactly the thing we have no",
    "way to measure and FPL's own data does not carry.",
    "",
    "WHY THIS EXISTS. FPL publishes one position per player, DEF, so the minutes",
    "allocation pooled all seven Arsenal defenders against 4.04 shirts. Timber",
    "being out therefore spread his minutes across centre-backs. With a role",
    "chart his share redistributes inside RB, which is where it actually goes.",
    "",
    "BASELINE, NOT AVAILABILITY-ADJUSTED. Timber is listed at 86% at RB while",
    "ruled out injured. That is the right layer for us: lib/minutes applies",
    "fitness on top and lib/xp applies per-fixture availability after that, so",
    "an injury must NOT already be priced in here or it would be counted twice.",
    "",
    "A player appears in as many slots as he is projected in — Eze at LW and LCM,",
    "Hincapie at LB and LCB. Do not flatten that; the slot is the whole point.",
    "",
    "STALE THE DAY IT IS LOADED. Everything else in site_data refreshes several",
    "times a day; this does not. `captured` is stamped so nothing downstream can",
    "mistake it for live data."
  ],
